let __v_1407 = Value::from("Your credit score is a number worked out from your credit report: what you owe, how much of each card limit you use, whether payments arrive on time and how long you have held accounts. Experian, Equifax and TransUnion each score it on a different scale, and a lender reads the report itself rather than the score, so the free report from all three is worth more than the number.");
frame.store("CREDIT_SCORE_IS", __v_1407.clone())?;
let __v_1408 = Value::from("There is no one good number, because the three agencies score on different scales: Experian runs from 0 to 999 and puts roughly 881 to 960 in its good band, Equifax scores out of 1,000 and TransUnion out of 710. What a lender weighs is the report behind the number - payments on time, card balances under about 30% of the limit and no run of new applications - so the band matters less than those three.");
frame.store("CREDIT_SCORE_GOOD", __v_1408.clone())?;
let __v_1409 = Value::from("Yes, and it is the mark that hurts most: a missed or late payment is recorded against that month on your credit report and stays visible for six years, though most of the damage fades within a year of on-time payments. Pay it as soon as you can and ask the lender to note the reason, set up a direct debit for at least the minimum so it cannot happen again, and keep every other payment on time - lenders read the last 12 months hardest. It does not reset the six years to start the clock again by paying it off.");
frame.store("CREDIT_SCORE_MISSED", __v_1409.clone())?;
