let __v_1553 = Value::from("Nothing is due below £325,000, or £650,000 for a married couple who leave everything to each other, and a home left to children adds up to £175,000 each on top. Gifts are the main lever: anything given more than seven years before the death is usually outside the estate, £3,000 a year is always free, and a wedding gift of up to £5,000 from a parent is too. Above the threshold the rate is 40% and it falls on the estate at death, not on a gift someone made while alive, so keep a written record of every gift and its date - the estate has to prove the seven years.");
