let __v_1605 = Value::from("Tell them the amount and the date in one message: \"I owe you £600, I can do £50 a week from Friday, so it's clear by March.\" Put it on a standing order so it happens without a conversation every month, and if you cannot pay this month say so before the date, not after - a small, steady repayment keeps the relationship and the debt honest.");
frame.store("_THE_DEBTOR_SCRIPT", __v_1605.clone())?;
let __v_1606 = Value::from("Say it once, plainly and in writing, and put a date on it: \"You said £200 by the end of the month - can you do the 30th?\" Naming the amount and a day is a request, not an accusation, and a message is easier than a face-to-face. If money is tight for them, agree a standing order of a small amount a week rather than another promise, and say what happens if it slips - that is what keeps the friendship and the money.");
